#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "September 2026 {#september-2026}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"New tools have been built on top of the [directed execution "
"model](/guides/directed-execution-model) framework, which was released "
"earlier this year:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-"
"learning) is a toolkit for randomization-based quantum noise "
"characterization. You can use it to construct a custom noise-learning "
"experiment, validate it with local simulation, and analyze the raw "
"results.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation)"
" is a package of quantum error mitigation methods for building mitigation "
"pipelines with the new execution model. It includes implementations of well-"
"known methods, including PEC, PEA, TREX, and gate-folding ZNE, as well as "
"post-selection for filtering out non-Markovian errors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "August 2026 {#august-2026}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Qiskit Fermions](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) had "
"its first release this month! This package provides tools for working with "
"fermionic systems, including building fermionic operators and circuits, "
"implementing fermion-to-qubit encodings, and circuit synthesis through the "
"Qiskit transpiler integration. Qiskit Fermions can be used with other "
"complementary tools in the ecosystem, such as `ffsim` (see this "
"[documentation](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and "
"[blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/ffsim) for more information) and the"
" [SQD addon](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), to build"
" advanced workflows for fermionic systems. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See how these tools are applied in practice with the [SqDRIFT algorithm for "
"ground state estimation](/tutorials/sqdrift) tutorial and the following "
"guide: [Building constant-depth circuits to simulate the dynamics of the 1- "
"and 2-D Fermi-Hubbard model](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-"
"fermions/guides/1-d-fermi-hubbard). Check out the "
"[blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-fermions) and "
"[documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-fermions) to get "
"started.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "June 2026 {#june-2026}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introducing [Qiskit Paulice](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-"
"addon-paulice): a new addon that integrates low-overhead quantum error "
"detection into quantum circuits to boost the fidelity of measured "
"distributions. It provides single-shot access to the quantum state and so "
"can be used in both sampling-based and expectation value-based workflows. "
"Check out the [blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qiskit-paulice) and "
"[documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-paulice) "
"for how to get started today.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Previous updates {#previous-updates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recently released two new addons that use classical resources to reduce "
"the quantum resources needed for error mitigation:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Propagated noise absorption (PNA)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-"
"pna/) is a technique for mitigating errors in expectation values by "
"absorbing the inverses of the learned noise channels into observables using "
"Pauli propagation. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [Shaded lightcones (SLC)](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/) "
"addon uses classical simulations to more tightly bound the sensitivity to "
"errors throughout the circuit. This allows for more efficient, targeted "
"applications of Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) with reduced "
"variance.\n"
msgstr ""
